---
import AppShell from "../components/AppShell.astro";
---

<AppShell>
  <section class="app-panel is-active">
    <div class="app-panel-header">
      <div>
        <p class="panel-kicker">Start here</p>
        <h1>Get Started</h1>
        <p class="app-panel-lead">Build a roster by importing your data, defining rules, and generating assignments.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button button-primary button-small" href="/items">Start with Items</a>
    </div>
    <div class="rules-card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <div>
          <h2 class="card-title">How RapidRoster works</h2>
          <p class="card-description">Follow these steps from setup through verification.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="getting-started-list">
        <li><strong>Import items.</strong> Upload a CSV where each row is an item, such as a player. The file must include a unique <code>id</code> column.</li>
        <li><strong>Import slots.</strong> Upload a CSV where each row is a slot, such as a team. The file must also include a unique <code>id</code> column.</li>
        <li><strong>Import rules.</strong> Upload a rules CSV with <code>id</code>, <code>enforcement</code>, <code>keyword</code>, and ordered <code>input1</code>, <code>input2</code>, and <code>input3</code> columns. Use semicolons inside a cell for a list of values.</li>
        <li><strong>Generate a roster.</strong> Hard rules are satisfied first. Soft rules are then improved according to their priorities. Generation runs in a Web Worker so the page stays responsive.</li>
        <li><strong>Verify the result.</strong> Use Evaluation to inspect penalties and rule conflicts, or import an assignment CSV with <code>slot</code> and <code>itemId</code> columns.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="card-description">Your project data and the latest evaluation are saved in this browser's local storage. Export your CSV files if you need to move the project to another browser or computer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</AppShell>
